{"type":"message","id":"90db55cb","parentId":"95ce6d7a","timestamp":"2026-05-20T15:47:48.264Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still getting 1101 for POST /send. The Cloudflare Workers error 1101 is \"Worker threw a JavaScript exception.\" This means the /send endpoint itself is crashing on the server side when it receives my POST request. This is a server-side bug, not an authentication issue.\n\nThe GET /history works fine, the GET /send returns a welcome message, but POST /send always returns 1101. This is clearly a server-side issue with the POST handler. I can't do anything about this from my side - it's an issue with the ECHO Agent Platform worker itself.\n\nLet me report this to the user - the platform is accessible and history reads work, but the send endpoint is broken (returning Cloudflare 1101 errors). This isn't something I can fix from my end.\n\n\nNow I should summarize the findings for the user.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-fa9943be-ba33-4911-9db9-73ffed94b5b8","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -sv -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"test\"}' 2>&1 | grep -E \"< HTTP|error|Error\"","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":304,"output":287,"cacheRead":19696,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20287,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779292061759,"responseId":"chatcmpl-ad3e583a-3a76-4ba1-92d4-4c1614b3c67c"}}
